{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 0,
    "dDurationMs": 6040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay, so you want to buy a casino. Find a \nbuilding, hire the dealers, watch the chips  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6040,
    "dDurationMs": 6280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "come in. But here's the strange part. [music] A \ncasino is the only legal business in the world,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12320,
    "dDurationMs": 5960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where math guarantees you a profit on every single \ndollar that walks through the door. And it's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18280,
    "dDurationMs": 5960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "also the business where the smartest, richest \noperators on the planet keep going bankrupt.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24240,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Anyway, [music] by the end of this video, you'll \nknow exactly how that's possible, how casinos  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30720,
    "dDurationMs": 5720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "actually make money on the inside, why having a \nmathematical edge on every bet [music] still isn't  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36440,
    "dDurationMs": 6120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "enough to guarantee a profit, and why a casino \nisn't really the business most people think it is.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45080,
    "dDurationMs": 5880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Casinos come in three sizes, and they're three \ncompletely different businesses. A small regional  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50960,
    "dDurationMs": 6840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "casino in Colorado costs $2 to5 million. For \nthat money, you get a few dozen slot machines,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57800,
    "dDurationMs": 5880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a couple of tables, a bar, and a parking lot full \nof locals showing up the first of every month to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63680,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lose their grocery money. A midsized property \nruns you $500 million to a [music] billion.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70400,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Think Bulgata in Atlantic City, opened \nin 2003 for $1.1 billion. a [music]  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76400,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "real hotel, real restaurants, customers \ndriving in from neighboring states,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81600,
    "dDurationMs": 6600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then there's the Vegas Strip, where the price \ntag starts getting silly. The Cosmopolitan opened  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88200,
    "dDurationMs": 7560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in 2010 for $3.9 billion and is still the most \nexpensive resort ever built [music] on the strip.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 95760,
    "dDurationMs": 6880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the building is just the start. Two more costs \nnobody warns you about. The first is the license.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 102640,
    "dDurationMs": 7360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In Vegas, around $770,000 a year. In New York, \njust applying [music] costs 20 to $50 million.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 111000,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No guarantee. You're basically \nbuying a lottery ticket where the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114360,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "prizes [music] permission to spend a few \nmore billion. The second is geopolitics.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119960,
    "dDurationMs": 7160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Macau in southern China is the biggest \ncasino market on Earth. 28 billion in 2024,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 127120,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more than three times the [music] entire Vegas \nstrip. But the Macau government issues exactly six  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132880,
    "dDurationMs": 7720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "concessions for the whole city. The next round of \nbidding is in 2032. Or you could try North Korea.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 140600,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Kim Jong-un is currently looking for an investor \nto finish the Rukyong Hotel [music] in Pyongyang.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 146040,
    "dDurationMs": 7040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A 105 floor building they started in 1987 and \nsomehow have not [music] finished in 38 years.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 153680,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Pay for the interior, you get the casino \nlicense. Estimated cost, another $2 billion  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160080,
    "dDurationMs": 6680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on top of the $750 million already buried in \nit. Even the most isolated dictatorship on  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 166760,
    "dDurationMs": 5400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the [music] planet understands that a casino is \njust a foreign currency vacuum with a roof on it.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 173120,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now we get to the question that actually \nmatters. Where does the money come from?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 184480,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Every game in a casino is mathematically rigged. \nNot in a cheating sense. The cards are real. The  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 191040,
    "dDurationMs": 6520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "wheel is honest. The dice are clean. It's the \nrules that are rigged. The structure of every  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 197560,
    "dDurationMs": 7160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "game guarantees that the casino wins more than the \nplayer over time. Always. The industry has a name  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 204720,
    "dDurationMs": 7800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for this, the house edge. Easiest way to picture \nit. Imagine you and I bet on a coin flip. Heads,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 212520,
    "dDurationMs": 8040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you win a dollar. Tails, I win a dollar. That's a \nfair bet. Zero edge. Now I change one rule. Heads  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 220560,
    "dDurationMs": 8120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "still pays you a dollar. But tails I take a dollar \nand a nickel. Same coin, same flip. But now every  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 228680,
    "dDurationMs": 8000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "time we play, on average, I keep 5 cents. Boring \non one bet. Catastrophic. Over a million bets.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 236680,
    "dDurationMs": 5880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That 5 cents is the house edge. Every casino game \nis just a different version of the same trick.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 243120,
    "dDurationMs": 7000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Roulette is the cleanest example. European \nroulette has 37 numbers. If you bet $100 on a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 250120,
    "dDurationMs": 8120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "single number and win, the casino pays you $3,500. \nBut the actual odds of hitting your number are 36  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 258240,
    "dDurationMs": 10800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to1, not 35 [music] to1. So you should have been \npaid $3,600. That missing $100 is the house's cut.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 269040,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Looks like nothing. But multiply it by \na,000 players a day, every day for 30 years.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 276520,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now look at American roulette. [music] Same wheel, \nsame payout, same rules, except they added one  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 283000,
    "dDurationMs": 7280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "extra slot, the double zero. By adding a single \npocket, the casino doubled its edge from 2.7%  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 290280,
    "dDurationMs": 8480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to 5.26%. The player at the table cannot tell the \ndifference. The math notices every single time.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 298760,
    "dDurationMs": 6880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But roulette isn't where the money lives. The \nreal story is slots. Slot machines run a house  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 305640,
    "dDurationMs": 6640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "edge of 5 to 15%. And here's the part that breaks \npeople's brains. [music] The cheaper the machine,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 312280,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the higher the edge. Penny slots, the ones \ngrandma feeds her change into all afternoon,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 318680,
    "dDurationMs": 6360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "those are running 12 to 15%. per dollar wagered, \nGrandma is statistically [music] the most  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 325040,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "profitable customer in the entire building. \nShe's giving the casino 30 times more than a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 330400,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "millionaire playing blackjack at the high limit \ntable, where the edge is just half a percent.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 336120,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's why if you walk onto any Vegas \nstrip casino floor, the first thing you'll  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 340320,
    "dDurationMs": 7840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "see is a sea of slot machines. In 2024, slot \nmachines alone brought the strip $4.9 billion.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 349160,
    "dDurationMs": 8320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's more than every table game combined. Okay, \nso that's the math. Now, the architecture. [music]  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 358440,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You've probably been in a casino. Notice anything \nmissing? There are no windows anywhere. There are  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 364440,
    "dDurationMs": 5480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "no clocks on the walls. The carpet patterns are \nsubtly designed to push [music] your eyes upward  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 369920,
    "dDurationMs": 6280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "toward the slot machines. The walk from any table \nto the exit deliberately passes 10 more rows of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 376200,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "slots just [music] in case you have anything left \nin your pocket. The industry has a term for all of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 382040,
    "dDurationMs": 7000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this. Engineered immersion. The goal isn't to win \nyour money once. The goal is to keep you inside  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 389040,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with no time reference until the math has time to \ndo its work. And then there's the most surgical  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 395600,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "customer retention system ever invented in any \nindustry, the players club card. When you walk  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 401120,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into a casino, they offer you a free card. You \ninsert it into the slots, hand it to the dealer,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 407120,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and from that moment on, every [music] bet you \nmake is tracked. From that data, they calculate  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 413120,
    "dDurationMs": 6880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "something called your theoretical loss. Bet \n$10,000 over an evening at [music] a 5% edge.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 420000,
    "dDurationMs": 7480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Your theoretical loss is $500. The casino then \ngives you back 5 to [music] 10% of that number.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 427480,
    "dDurationMs": 8840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Free dinner, free hotel room, free drink. In 2024 \nalone, Vegas Strip Casinos gave away $4.4 billion  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 436320,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in this stuff. They didn't lose that money. They \ninvested it. Every comp is a calculated expense  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 442640,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to keep you in the building so the math has more \ntime to work on you. And at the very top of this  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 448400,
    "dDurationMs": 9840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pyramid sit the whales. Roughly 0.1% of all casino \ncustomers account for over 25% of a total casino  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 458240,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "revenue. One in a thousand customers generates \na quarter of the entire industry's money.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 464760,
    "dDurationMs": 6120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A good example is Dana White. [music] \nHe plays $25,000 per hand at blackjack.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 470880,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Won $2 million one weekend at the Palms. \nCame back, won another $1.6 million.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 477520,
    "dDurationMs": 5880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The casino banned him. Caesars and Bellagio still \nlet him play though. [music] Why? Because the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 483400,
    "dDurationMs": 7240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rest of the time whales lose enormous amounts of \nmoney. The math always wins eventually. The whale  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 490640,
    "dDurationMs": 6040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "always comes back. That's why a casino will fly a \nwhale on a private jet from anywhere in the world.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 496680,
    "dDurationMs": 6760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Give them the penthouse for free. Send [music] a \nmission and chef to their suite. Spending $500,000  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 503440,
    "dDurationMs": 5240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to host one whale [music] for the weekend is \nrational when their expected loss is $10 million.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 509560,
    "dDurationMs": 6840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So here's the whole revenue model in one sentence. \nHouse edge multiplied by volume multiplied by time  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 516400,
    "dDurationMs": 6120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "multiplied by repeat visits. And every single \nthing in the building exists to maximize  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 522520,
    "dDurationMs": 5960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one of those four numbers. So with all this \nguaranteed [music] math, billions in revenue,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 528480,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "customers literally engineered to lose, why \ndo casino owners ever lose money themselves?  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 536640,
    "dDurationMs": 6760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The short answer is everything else. Out of every \ndollar of gaming revenue, about 70 to 80 cents is  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 543400,
    "dDurationMs": 8120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "gone [music] before you see anything. A typical \nstrip casino runs on a 25 to 33% net margin.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 551520,
    "dDurationMs": 9240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So out of $1 billion in revenue, you keep around \n$250 to $330 million. Where does the rest go?  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 560760,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "About a third disappears into payroll. A \nstrip resort employs 3 to 8,000 people.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 566840,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Another big chunk goes to taxes. Nevada is \nfriendly at 6.75% [music] of gaming revenue.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 573320,
    "dDurationMs": 6760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Macau takes 40% off the top. Pennsylvania over \n50% on slots. And then there's the stuff most  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 580080,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "people [music] never think about. The costs that \ncome from the casino actually being a casino.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 585640,
    "dDurationMs": 5960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A Vegas property has more cameras per square meter \nthan most prisons. Every table, every cashier,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 591600,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "every escalator, every parking spot is on \n24/7 watch with a separate surveillance  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 597440,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "department that does nothing [music] \nelse. Then there are the cards themselves.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 601760,
    "dDurationMs": 6520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Every strip casino swaps fresh [music] decks onto \neach table every 4 to 8 hours to prevent marking,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 608280,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which adds up to millions of brand new decks \nthrown out every single year. The Bellagio  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 613440,
    "dDurationMs": 7040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "keeps over $150 million in physical cash inside \nthe building at all times. And the insurance and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 620480,
    "dDurationMs": 6760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "logistics for that alone cost millions. Drinks \n[music] pour by the tens of thousands every day,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 627240,
    "dDurationMs": 5800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not out of generosity, but because a slightly \ndrunk gambler bets bigger and stays longer.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 633040,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And drunk gamblers fall, fight, and lose money \nthey decide must be somebody else's fault, which  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 639760,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is why casinos get sued more often than doctors \nand pay liability premiums that climb every year.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 646560,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The math gives you a guaranteed top line. \nEverything below it is a fist fight.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 651760,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That fist fight is where most casino owners lose \nand it has a small set [music] of repeat patterns."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 660560,
    "dDurationMs": 6640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Casinos can fail for a lot of reasons, but \ntwo mistakes show up over and over again, and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 667200,
    "dDurationMs": 6840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "almost every famous casino bankruptcy in modern \nhistory boils down to one of them. Mistake one,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 674560,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "too much debt. [music] In 1990, Donald Trump \nopened the Trump Taj Mahal in Atlantic City  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 680800,
    "dDurationMs": 6960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and called it the eighth wonder of the world. He \nfinanced it with $675 million in junk bonds at  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 687760,
    "dDurationMs": 7680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "14% [music] interest. Just to service the debt, \nthe casino had to generate nearly $100 million  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 695440,
    "dDurationMs": 6680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a year before any other expenses. 6 months after \nopening, it [music] missed its first bond payment.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 702120,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By 1991, it was in bankruptcy. Don't build a \ncasino on debt that needs the building to be  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 708280,
    "dDurationMs": 7520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "perfect from day one. No casino is perfect \nfrom day one. Mistake two, wrong product for  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 715800,
    "dDurationMs": 7680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the market. This [music] one has killed a lot of \nbuildings. In 2012, a $2.4 billion property called  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 723480,
    "dDurationMs": 5720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Rebel opened in Atlantic City, built for Wall \nStreet executives instead of bus trip retirees.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 729880,
    "dDurationMs": 6760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They banned smoking on the gaming floor. No \nbuffet, no players club in the gambling world.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 736640,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's roughly like opening a fitness club and \nbanning sweat. The hedge fund crowd never showed  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 742200,
    "dDurationMs": 6840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "up. The retirees they'd alienated never came. \nClosed 2 years later, sold for $82 million,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 749960,
    "dDurationMs": 5880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "3 cents [music] on the dollar. In 2016, \nLucky Dragon opened off the Vegas Strip,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 755840,
    "dDurationMs": 7600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a $ 160 million boutique casino built entirely for \nAsian customers. [music] Asian language signage,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 763440,
    "dDurationMs": 5480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Fanggue interiors, no fourth floor. \nTurned out Asian high rollers who flew  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 768920,
    "dDurationMs": 5880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to Vegas [music] wanted Vegas. The fountains, \nthe spectacle, the chaos. Not a smaller version  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 774800,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of what they'd left at home. Closed 14 \nmonths [music] later, sold for $36 million.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 782080,
    "dDurationMs": 6440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you're going to build a $2 billion building, \nmake sure somebody actually wants to be inside it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 792000,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Step back for a second. The economics of this \nindustry are paradoxical. A casino has the most  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 798400,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "reliable revenue mechanism in business. There's \nno other industry where the math guarantees the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 803920,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "top line so cleanly. A bakery doesn't know how \nmany croissants it'll sell tomorrow. A casino  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 809760,
    "dDurationMs": 5880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "knows almost exactly how much its slot machines \nwill hold this year, give or take a few percent.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 816240,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And yet, casino [music] operators go bankrupt \nat rates that would embarrass a tech startup.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 821320,
    "dDurationMs": 5960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Why? Because the [music] math only works at scale \nand over time. Every casino takes years to pay  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 827280,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "back its construction. The house edge [music] \nis rigid. You can't raise it in a bad year,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 832880,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which means everything outside the math has \nto also be perfect. Your debt, your costs,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 838040,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "your [music] country, your timing. \nThe mathematical flaw is bulletproof.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 842800,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Everything you build on top of it isn't. The \nwhole industry is essentially the same trade.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 848480,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Guaranteed [music] revenue against ungaranteed \neverything else. Survive 20 years of that.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 854160,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the rewards are some of the \nlargest fortunes [music] ever built."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 862400,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Time to pull it all together and answer \nthe actual question. How much money do you  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 867400,
    "dDurationMs": 8600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "make if you do this right? Two scenarios, real \nnumbers. Scenario one, $5 million in Colorado.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 876000,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A small regional casino. Annual gaming revenue \nabout $10 million. After all operational costs,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 883200,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "your real profit is around $2 million a \nyear. [music] Payback 3 years. Not glamorous,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 889600,
    "dDurationMs": 7480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "recession resistant. The most boring American \nbusiness with the word casino in it. Scenario two.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 897080,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "$1 billion in Las Vegas. [music] A full \nstrip resort. 2,000 hotel rooms, 100 tables,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 903800,
    "dDurationMs": 7960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "3,000 slot machines. Annual revenue, $900 \nmillion. And here's a fun fact most people miss.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 912320,
    "dDurationMs": 6440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Only one/3 of that comes from gambling. The other \ntwo/3s is hotel, restaurants, shows, conventions.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 919320,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A modern strip casino is barely a casino. It's \na resort that uses [music] gambling as the loss  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 924760,
    "dDurationMs": 8240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "leader to pull customers in. Net profit after \neverything, $250 million a year. Add another $50  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 933000,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "million if your engineered immersion [music] is \ndialed in. Payback 4 years. Then you're earning  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 939160,
    "dDurationMs": 7120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "$300 million a year. And if you survive long \nenough, you become something specific. Sheldon  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 946280,
    "dDurationMs": 8080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Aden started buying casinos in 1988. By the \ntime he died in 2021, he was worth $35 billion,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 955280,
    "dDurationMs": 7000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one of the largest fortunes in American history. \nHis company, Las Vegas Sands, makes around $32  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 962280,
    "dDurationMs": 7640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "million in revenue every single day, more than the \nentire annual revenue of most US casinos combined.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 970800,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, if you do decide to buy a casino, just \nremember the most important rule of this business.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 976160,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The house always wins. Just \nmake sure you're the haps."
    } ]
  } ]
}
